  "date": "2026-10-20",
  "category": "finance",
  "title_zh": "十月贷款利率不变，已经连续17个月没有调整",
  "title_en": "October Loan Prime Rate Unchanged — No Adjustment for 17 Months in a Row",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "zh": "10月20日，中国公布了最新的贷款市场报价利率（LPR）。1年期LPR是3.0%，5年期以上LPR是3.5%，都和上个月一样。这已经是LPR连续第17个月保持不变。",
      "en": "On October 20, China announced its latest Loan Prime Rate (LPR). The 1-year LPR is 3.0% and the 5-year-and-above LPR is 3.5%, both the same as last month. This is the 17th month in a row that the LPR has stayed unchanged."
    },
    {
      "zh": "LPR是银行给企业和个人发放贷款时参考的利率，其中5年期以上LPR和房贷关系最密切。LPR主要根据央行的政策利率来决定，而这个政策利率从2025年5月以后就没有变过，所以这次LPR也没有变化。",
      "en": "The LPR is the reference rate banks use when lending to companies and individuals; the 5-year-and-above LPR is the one most closely tied to mortgages. The LPR is mainly based on the central bank's policy rate, which hasn't changed since May 2025, so the LPR didn't change this time either."
    },
    {
      "zh": "10月19日，央行行长潘功胜在金融街论坛上表示，以后要更多地发挥利率的作用。他还说，贷款利率的定价标准将从只参考LPR，慢慢变得更加多样化。",
      "en": "On October 19, central bank governor Pan Gongsheng said at the Financial Street Forum that interest rates should play a bigger role in the future. He also said the pricing benchmark for loans will gradually move from relying only on the LPR to becoming more diversified."
    },
    {
      "zh": "对普通人来说，利率不变意味着房贷和其他贷款的成本暂时不会降低。",
      "en": "For ordinary people, unchanged rates mean that the cost of mortgages and other loans won't come down for now."
    }
  ],
